.TH io_eagain_write 3
.SH NAME
io_eagain_write \- signal that a file descriptor is not ready for writing

.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <io.h>

void \fBio_eagain_write\fP(fd_type \fId\fP);

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B io_eagain_write
marks the file descriptor \fId\fP as currently unable to accept further data for writing. 
This function should be called when a write operation on the file descriptor returns
an error code indicating that the resource is temporarily unavailable (e.g., EAGAIN or EWOULDBLOCK).

Internally, this updates the IO management structure to reflect that \fId\fP's
write readiness state is false. If the system is using a signal-based IO multiplexing
mechanism (like SIGIO), it also performs the necessary queue management to remove the
descriptor from the alternative write queue.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I d
The file descriptor to be marked as not ready for writing.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR io_wait (3),
.BR io_canwrite (3),
.BR io_trywrite (3)